<title>GERMANY: German grain trade seeks intervention rye export.</title>
<headline>German grain trade seeks intervention rye export.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids for the export of 90,128 tonnes of intervention rye to third countries at the European Union's weekly grain export tender, state intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The total included multiple bids for identical lots, BLE said.</p>
<p>The net volume was 50,910 tonnes.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
